SUMMARY:[Faculty Staff Help Center] AI and Mental Health: Clinical and Eth
 ical Considerations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T131500
DTSTAMP:20261008T191016Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53819963831081-53819963831082@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Increasingly considered as a possible means of supporting ther
 apist training or extending between-session support to patients\, AI is al
 so being evaluated as a stand-alone mental health intervention. Although t
 he field is advancing\, demonstrating that AI can be deployed safely\, eff
 ectively\, and equitably poses substantial challenges. In this presentatio
 n\, Shannon Wiltsey Stirman\, PhD\, will review how LLM–based tools are 
 currently being applied across mental health care and address consideratio
 ns\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-08 12:10 PDT
END:VEVENT
