SUMMARY:[Center on Democracy\, Development and the Rule of Law / The Europ
 e Center] Aleksandar Matovski — The Kremlin’s Pressure Cooker: Restrai
 nt and Escalation in Russia’s War on Ukraine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T131500
DTSTAMP:20261008T191016Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54003656864145-54003807198993@local-events
DESCRIPTION:As Russia’s war against Ukraine grinds on and debate intensi
 fies over how to end it\, what could push the conflict into a more dangero
 us phase of escalation? This talk examines how the Putin regime’s domest
 ic political imperatives shape when Moscow absorbs setbacks and when it es
 calates. It argues that Russian behavior reflects a “pressure-cooker” 
 dynamic: external geopolitical constraints favor restraint\, while battlef
 ield failures\, war weariness\, and pressure from hardliners can gradually
  raise\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://cddrl.fsi.stanford.edu/events/al
 eksandar-matovski-kremlins-pressure-cooker-restraint-and-escalation-russia
 s-war-ukraine\nLast synced: 2026-10-08 12:10 PDT
