BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Environmental Social Sciences / Stanford Doerr School of Sustaina
 bility] Global Environmental Policy Seminar with Guojun He
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T143000
DTSTAMP:20261008T191016Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53701670896871-53701670897896@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Carbon Markets with Chinese Characteristics: From Design to Co
 nsequences \n\nThis paper studies the design and consequences of China’s
  national rate-based carbon market. Under this system\, emission‑intensi
 ty benchmarks create implicit subsidies for cleaner plants and taxes for d
 irtier ones\, rotating the supply curve without changing the merit order. 
 A theoretical model shows that\, combined with strategic bidding and relat
 ively loose benchmarks\, this design weakens incentives to pass carbon cos
 ts t\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-08 12:10 PDT
LOCATION:Y2E2 Building
END:VEVENT
