BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Center for East Asian Studies / Department of East Asian Language
 s and Cultures] Best Friend or Cyber Mother? A Confucian Reflection on AI 
 Companionship
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T153000
DTSTAMP:20261008T191016Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53790043944392-53790043944393@local-events
DESCRIPTION:AI companions designed to simulate romantic or friendly intima
 cy are rapidly expanding\, but most critiques remain framed by Western lib
 eral assumptions. I develop an alternative critique grounded in Confucian 
 ethics. It begins by challenging the industry claim that AI companions off
 er a remedy for loneliness. Against this view\, I argue that Confucianism 
 values positive solitude as a condition of self-cultivation and a precondi
 tion for genuine friendship. I further argue that AI companions are be\n\n
 Ages: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-08 12:10 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
END:VEVENT
